kisaru is a modified version of the program "qs-novelmangareader", originally
published by dhrruvsharma at

    https://github.com/dhrruvsharma/qs-novelmangareader

Original work: Copyright (C) dhrruvsharma and contributors, licensed under
GPL-3.0. Its copyright notices are retained in the source files.

Modification date: the work was forked on 2026-10-07 at upstream commit
c3ebeca ("fix: Fixing commands not working with users not having local bin in
their path"), and has been modified continuously since then.

Modification range: all commits of this repository after that base commit,
starting with commit eb39f81 ("chore: initialize i18n-es workspace and feature
plan", 2026-10-11) on the branch i18n-es. To see the complete set of changes
against the original work:

    git clone https://github.com/pwn27sbx/kisaru
    git remote add upstream https://github.com/dhrruvsharma/qs-novelmangareader
    git fetch upstream
    git log --patch c3ebeca..origin/i18n-es

Summary of the modifications:

  * Spanish interface (all labels, buttons, states and error messages) with a
    persisted EN/ES toggle, and Spanish content sources for anime, manga and
    novels, as two independent preferences.
  * Adoption of the Omarchy shell: the panels take theme, typography, radii and
    control components from qs.Commons and qs.Ui instead of carrying their own
    copy, and the app warns when the Omarchy version line changes.
  * A single shared component layer for the three panels: header with tabs and
    counts, search field, filter chips, cover card, list row, loading skeleton,
    settings view and view-mode toggle.
  * Per-panel grid/list view, remembered in settings.json, and a settings page
    for scroll speed, interface language and audio mode.
  * Extensive test suites (Node for the QML-side modules and the CLI, Python
    unittest for the local backends) and linting tools for style and i18n.
  * Source chain hardening for manga (MangaDex, InManga, ZonaTMO, ManhwaWeb,
    WeebCentral) and a local image proxy.

The project is distributed as "kisaru". Its configuration directory, command,
bar widget, data paths and caches use that name; the IPC targets
(animePlayer, mangaReader, novelReader) keep their original names.
